CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ element 2 is found: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ found element has the searched value: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^.*is unknown.*$
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^.*no body for callee.*$
--
std::find over a populated std::vector verifies genuinely once the iterator
instance's member functions are instantiated on demand ([iterator.concepts.general]
+ [temp.inst]/1-2 + [dcl.typedef]: the inert C++20 `iterator_concept` member
alias is kept lazy instead of abandoning the iterator's class body and dropping
its operator*/operator++/comparison members).  The forbidden patterns guard
against the prior method-less-iterator regression and against a vacuous pass;
the assertion-SUCCESS lines require the search result to be checked exactly.
